[p][/p][p][b]Hello, Cowboys! Announcement #21[/b] [b]Dev News[/b] [/p][p][b]Episode 1 Maps[/b][/p][p]In this announcement, we will try out the early-stage technical versions of three new maps, so that you can see the rendering process from the very first stage. 
The list of new locations includes: 

1.The Oblivion Valley (ANIMA/STEEL) 
2.The Black River (ANIMA) 
3.Hellish Chasm (STEEL) [/p][p][b][i]Bugfixes[/i][/b][/p][p] ●The color scheme of notifications and target information have been adjusted;
 ●The targeting system now works more stably at long distances; ●You can now see the distance to the target; 
●The sounds of skills and various notifications has been significantly changed; 
●The direction of knockback and velocity slowdown upon collision now work correctly;
●New visual effects for incoming damage to the shield and energy have been added;
●The auto-horizon work is almost complete. Significant progress has been made; 
●The roll fixes are in their final stage. We are still missing some numbers that would work just perfectly but we are close; 
●The BG and IG CS, Rampage, and Invisible skills have received new sounds and animations;
●The MG Reverse Engine skill has been fixed; 
●The radar tab has been completely redesigned; 
●You no longer fall underground after death; 
●GBM/ABM work is actively underway and we have made good progress;
●B+Enter now works more smoothly; 
The missile reload display has been fixed; 
●Defensive skills now reduce incoming damage correctly; 
●The inventory no longer opens on the fly, so that this is not used as an advantage in the future; ●Changing targets with SHIFT now works correctly; 
●ALT+TAB no longer leads to critical errors during various events in the game; 
●The problem with missiles spinning around when capturing a target at an acute angle is almost solved; ●The color scheme for visualizing the map border has been reworked; 
●The acceleration smoothness after a roll has been changed, now this game element feels more comfortable; 
●FoV changes: now all skills are displayed correctly upon activation; 
●The camera and game menu for weaker PCs have been optimized; 
●Some smoke and explosion effects have been fixed. [/p][p][b]Additional information[/b][/p][p] Announcement #22 is scheduled for September 22, 2025 Full Video: [/p][p][dynamiclink href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yVSnTCZpSLg"][/dynamiclink][/p][p] (available now) Shorts-1 [/p][p][dynamiclink href="https://youtube.com/shorts/0u3empx0Ijw"][/dynamiclink][/p][p] (available now) Shorts-2 [/p][p][dynamiclink href="https://youtube.com/shorts/0RA6x5o9Fhg"][/dynamiclink][/p][p] (available 15.09) Shorts-3 [/p][p][dynamiclink href="https://youtube.com/shorts/MIL1EdpzxFc"][/dynamiclink][/p][p] (available 22.09)[/p]
